# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Historical slice-3 refusal, recovered by SOURCE-DECLARATION-ORDER19.
# addN's bare Counter resolves the existing source-owned callable body;
# defining Counter does not execute it. Preserve this program and its name.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + 1U
return
fn: makeAdder (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        Counter
        return: k + x
    return: addN

@: add makeAdder(5)
int: a (add: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
